    "created_at": "2015-11-23T15:22:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-23T15:22:18Z",
    "body": "Is the Gecko implementation pretty much step-by-step identical to the spec? If so I can see why it would complicate matters. In Blink there's first a search for the internal index of the attribute to replace, so the structure is quite different.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
