    "created_at": "2016-01-01T14:12:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-01T14:12:11Z",
    "body": "Judging from https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/9061#issuecomment-167796252 all browsers have a \"replace\" algorithm here and issue a single mutation record. Gecko just implements the replacing via remove/append, whereas everyone else does an actual replace. Given that we should just do the replacing thing. Adjusting @nox' PR will get us there.\n",
